# FedML Cervical Cytology with Noise2Noise & CycleGAN Preprocessing

A clinical-grade Federated Learning suite built with **FedML**, featuring dual advanced cellular preprocessing: **Noise2Noise (N2N)** blind sensor denoising and **CycleGAN** unpaired inter-clinic stain harmonization. Supports both **fastai** and **skorch** deep learning backends, 3 federated aggregation algorithms (**FedAvg**, **FedProx**, **FedAdam**), multi-candidate **Random Best Select** seed optimization (strictly rejecting seed 42), comprehensive performance evaluation metrics, and 5 environment managers (**Pixi**, **uv**, **Conda**, **venv**, **Pyenv**).

---

## 🔬 Architecture & Preprocessing Pipeline Overview

```
                      [Raw Cervical Micrographs]
                                  │
                                  ▼
                     ┌─────────────────────────┐
                     │ Stage 1: Noise2Noise    │  (Suppress optical & sensor noise;
                     │ Denoising (U-Net)       │   preserve chromatin texture)
                     └────────────┬────────────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
                     ┌─────────────────────────┐
                     │ Stage 2: CycleGAN Stain │  (Harmonize inter-clinic Papanicolaou
                     │ Normalization (ResNet)  │   stain variations across silos)
                     └────────────┬────────────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
                   [Restored Standardized Cytology]
                                  │
       ┌──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┐
       │                                                     │
       ▼                                                     ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐                           ┌─────────────────────────┐
│ Hospital Client Silo 01 │                           │ Hospital Client Silo 02 │
│  (Local fastai/skorch)  │                           │  (Local fastai/skorch)  │
└────────────┬────────────┘                           └────────────┬────────────┘
             │                                                     │
             └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
                                        ▼
                         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
                         │ FedML Central Server        │
                         │ Aggregator (FedAvg/Prox)    │
                         └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                                        ▼
                         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
                         │ Centralized Holdout Eval    │
                         │ (11 Clinical & Preproc Q)   │
                         └─────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 📊 Preprocessing Techniques

| Preprocessing Flag | Description | Primary Medical Utility |
|---|---|---|
| `--preprocessing none` | Raw unaltered cytology tiles | Baseline control for ablation studies |
| `--preprocessing n2n` | Noise2Noise blind restoration | Removes sensor/shot noise without ground-truth scans; enhances chromatin granulometry |
| `--preprocessing cyclegan` | Unpaired ResNet stain harmonizer | Eliminates inter-institutional color drift from varying Papanicolaou dye batches |
| `--preprocessing n2n_cyclegan` | Dual sequential pipeline | First removes optical artifacts, then unifies stain distributions across hospital silos |

---

## 📈 Comprehensive Performance Evaluation Metrics

### Clinical Classification Metrics
1. **Accuracy**: Overall prediction correctness.
2. **Balanced Accuracy**: Macro-average recall across all 7 diagnostic classes (robust to class imbalance).
3. **Macro & Weighted Precision**: Positive predictive value across diagnostic categories.
4. **Macro & Weighted Recall / Sensitivity**: Detection rate of dysplastic/malignant cells.
5. **Macro Specificity**: Rate of correctly identified true negatives across all cell classes.
6. **Macro & Weighted F1-Score**: Harmonic mean of precision and recall.
7. **Cohen's Kappa ($\kappa$)**: Inter-rater agreement accounting for chance agreement.
8. **Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC)**: High-quality metric for imbalanced multi-class evaluations.
9. **Macro AUC-ROC (One-vs-Rest)**: Class-separable discriminative capability.
10. **Log-Loss (Cross-Entropy)**: Uncertainty and probabilistic calibration.

### Micrograph Restoration & Quality Metrics
11. **PSNR (Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio in dB)**: Logarithmic measure of signal reconstruction fidelity.
12. **SSIM (Structural Similarity Index)**: Preservation of structural texture, luminance, and contrast.
13. **Shannon Distribution Entropy**: Information density and chromatin detail richness.

---

## 🚀 Quickstart

### Option 1: Pixi (Recommended)
```powershell
# Install & run full pipeline with dual preprocessing
pixi run test-dual

# Run comparative benchmark across all 4 preprocessing strategies
pixi run compare
```

### Option 2: Conda
```powershell
conda activate cervical_cells_fedml_n2n_cyclegan
python main_federated_fedml.py --preprocessing n2n_cyclegan --framework fastai
```

### Option 3: uv
```powershell
uv run python main_federated_fedml.py --preprocessing n2n_cyclegan --framework skorch
```

---

## ⚙️ CLI Reference

```
python main_federated_fedml.py [OPTIONS]

  --config PATH               Path to base TOML config file (default: configs/default.toml)
  --preprocessing MODE        Preprocessing pipeline: none | n2n | cyclegan | n2n_cyclegan
  --framework FW              Deep learning backend: fastai | skorch (default: fastai)
  --strategy STRAT            FedML aggregation strategy: FedAvg | FedProx | FedAdam
  --rounds INT                Federated communication rounds (default: 5)
  --clients INT               Decentralized hospital silos (default: 5)
  --epochs INT                Local client training epochs (default: 2)
  --lr FLOAT                  Local learning rate (default: 0.0003)
  --seed INT                  Explicit random seed (replaces 42 if specified)
  --random_best_select        Enable multi-candidate Random Best Select seed search (default: true)
  --candidates INT            Number of cryptographic seed candidates evaluated (default: 5)
  --subsample INT             Limit samples per silo for fast testing / dry runs
  --no_wandb                  Disable Weights & Biases logging
```

